From f3910e89d8e442be1489f267f679c3c10f2ef467 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:23:06 +0000
Subject: net: ethernet: lantiq: add datapath manager API layer

Add the datapath manager, the vendor abstraction that glues netdev
drivers to the CBM and the switch:

 - datapath_api.c: dp_init_module() (fired once after both switch
   instances have probed), the dp_alloc_port / dp_register_subif /
   dp_register_dev chain with its port/subif state machine, and the
   instance lookup helpers. dp_get_inst_via_module accepts ports in
   PORT_SUBIF_REGISTERED state and checks the per-port info table
   (not the instance storage) so re-registration after ndo_stop /
   ndo_open cycles works.

 - datapath_misc.c: the GSWIP-3.0 capability registration,
   dma-pmac template initialization and the queue-map programming
   helper used at subif registration.

 - datapath_instance.c: the minimal per-instance registry.

 - Headers: the public dp_* API surface and the GSWIP-3.0
   parameter blocks, reduced to the subset this port exercises.

The datapath calls into the CBM port-allocation surface
(cbm_dp_port_alloc/cbm_dp_enable, added in the next patch) and back
into the switch HAL via gsw_get_swcore_ops().

Derived from the AVM FRITZ!Box 7560 GPL release (Linux 4.9.198),
datapath/ - Copyright (C) Intel Corporation, Author: Shao Guohua
<guohua.shao@intel.com>; notices restored to all nine derived
files. Switchdev/QoS/PPA surfaces are not ported.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
